	"docs.articles.adventure-mcp.if-a-link-response-is-lost-retry-the":
		'If a link response is lost, retry the same character, CODE slot, server, and <span class="dlabel">request_id</span>. Do not invent a new request ID for a network retry. Disconnecting disables renewal but does not refund or pause remaining paid time.',
	// docs/articles/adventure-mcp.html:348; Documentation p prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Fixed HTML: preserve every tag, attribute, handler and URL exactly; translate visible prose only. Locked inline code: ["start_character","stop_character"]. Keep names: ["CODE","Mainframe"].
	"docs.articles.adventure-mcp.inside-running-code-start-character-can-add-up":
		'Inside running CODE, <span class="dlabel">start_character</span> can add up to three owned characters as included workers in the caller\'s shared machine, for four characters total. Each uses a separate CODE slot, game session, Worker identity, memory limit, and realm-limit authentication, but all share the root character\'s prepaid window and fixed machine CPU budget. The first child start reconnects the root once while Mainframe changes machine type. Later workers can start without replacing that shared machine. <span class="dlabel">stop_character</span> stops only that child; disconnecting the root stops every included character. Direct Mainframe links remain separate machines and separate charges.',
	// docs/articles/adventure-mcp.html:286; Documentation li prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Keep names: ["CODE"].
