	"docs.functions.require_code.exports-the-loaded-file-must-explicitly-assign-module":
		"<b>Exports:</b> The loaded file must explicitly assign <span class='dlabel'>module.exports</span> or add properties to <span class='dlabel'>exports</span>. Local declarations alone are not exported. Assigning <span class='dlabel'>exports = value</span> does not replace <span class='dlabel'>module.exports</span>. JavaScript <span class='dlabel'>import</span> and <span class='dlabel'>export</span> declarations are not supported.",
	// docs/functions/require_code.html:6; Documentation p prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Fixed HTML: preserve every tag, attribute, handler and URL exactly; translate visible prose only.
	"docs.functions.require_code.no-circular-dependencies-a-requiring-b-while-b":
		"<b>No circular dependencies:</b> A requiring B while B requires A keeps loading recursively until an error or execution limit stops it. Put shared values in a module that does not require its callers.",
	// docs/functions/require_code.html:5; Documentation p prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Fixed HTML: preserve every tag, attribute, handler and URL exactly; translate visible prose only.
	"docs.functions.require_code.no-module-cache-every-call-executes-the-file":
		"<b>No module cache:</b> Every call executes the file again, including nested calls from other modules. Objects created by separate executions are separate copies, and initialization can create duplicate timers or listeners. Require once and pass the returned value to callers that need the same object.",
	// docs/functions/require_code.html:3; Documentation p prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Fixed HTML: preserve every tag, attribute, handler and URL exactly; translate visible prose only.
	"docs.functions.require_code.returns-exports-object-or-any-value-assigned-to": "<b>Returns:</b> Exports object or any value assigned to module.exports.",
