	// docs/functions/start_character.html:7; Documentation p prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Fixed HTML: preserve every tag, attribute, handler and URL exactly; translate visible prose only. Locked inline code: ["stop_character(name)"]. Keep names: ["CODE","Mainframe"].
	"docs.functions.start_character.at-the-next-renewal-one-shell-or-free":
		"At the next renewal, one Shell or free Steam hour buys 60, 50, 45, or 40 minutes when 1, 2, 3, or 4 characters are active. Starting or stopping a child does not reprice the current window. If the root disconnects or cannot renew, every included worker stops. Use <span class='dlabel'>stop_character(name)</span> to stop only one child. Mainframe rejects a fifth character, a character active elsewhere, an unknown CODE slot, or a character from another account.",
	// docs/functions/start_character.html:8; Documentation p prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Fixed HTML: preserve every tag, attribute, handler and URL exactly; translate visible prose only.
	"docs.functions.start_character.example": "<b>Example:</b>",
	// docs/functions/start_character.html:6; Documentation p prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Fixed HTML: preserve every tag, attribute, handler and URL exactly; translate visible prose only. Keep names: ["CODE","Mainframe"].
	"docs.functions.start_character.mainframe-the-first-child-call-changes-the-caller":
		"<b>Mainframe:</b> The first child call changes the caller from a dedicated machine to a shared machine and can briefly reconnect it. Up to three other owned characters can run as included workers, for four characters total. Each uses its own CODE slot, game session, Worker identity, memory limit, and realm-limit authentication, but shares the root character's prepaid Mainframe window and fixed machine CPU budget. Starting the same character directly from the Mainframe page remains the more isolated, separately charged option.",
	// docs/functions/start_character.html:5; Documentation p prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Fixed HTML: preserve every tag, attribute, handler and URL exactly; translate visible prose only.
	"docs.functions.start_character.notes-repeated-calls-for-the-same-local-character":
		"<b>Notes:</b> Repeated calls for the same local character share its startup or reuse its active runner instead of creating duplicates.",
	// docs/functions/start_character.html:4; Documentation p prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Fixed HTML: preserve every tag, attribute, handler and URL exactly; translate visible prose only. Locked inline code: ["failed: true","reason","mode_resolve_all()"].
	"docs.functions.start_character.promise-failures-unless-a-function-specific-note-says":
		"<b>Promise failures:</b> Unless a function-specific note says otherwise, failures reject with an object containing <span class='dlabel'>failed: true</span> and a <span class='dlabel'>reason</span>. After <span class='dlabel'>mode_resolve_all()</span>, the same failures fulfill instead.",
	// docs/functions/start_character.html:3; Documentation p prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Fixed HTML: preserve every tag, attribute, handler and URL exactly; translate visible prose only.
	"docs.functions.start_character.returns-promise-resolving-when-the-character-is-running":
		"<b>Returns:</b> Promise resolving when the character is running, or immediately when it already has a local runner. Rejects when the name or slot is invalid, the character is already active elsewhere, startup is interrupted, or the timeout expires.",
	// docs/functions/start_character.html:2; Documentation p prose block. Keep Adventure Land, CODE symbols, and item/NPC/map/monster names unchanged. Keep names: ["CODE"].
	"docs.functions.start_character.starts-another-character-from-your-account-in-code": "Starts another character from your account in CODE-only mode, optionally with a code slot or file name.",
